.TH HELIKODU-CLI 1 2026-11-18 Helikodu "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helikodu\-cli \- play audio files, query the Helikodu library and control the application from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helikodu\-cli play
.IR file \&...
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli list\-outputs
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR backend ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli scan
.RI [ folder \&...]
.RB [ \-\-exclude
.IR pattern ]\&...
.RB [ \-\-workers
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-worker
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli search
.IR text \&...
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-offset
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli info
.IR file | track-id
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli stats
.RB [ \-\-top
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli loudness
.RB [ \-\-album | \-\-library ]
.RB [ \-\-write\-tags ]
.RB [ \-\-threads
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-worker
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.RI [ file | track-id ...]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli duplicates
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli import
.I player
.RB [ \-\-path
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-map
.IR from = to ]...
.RB [ \-\-replace\-ratings ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-playlists ]
.RB [ \-\-preview | \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli undo\-import
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli export\-user\-data
.I file
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli import\-user\-data
.I file
.RB [ \-\-map
.IR from = to ]...
.RB [ \-\-replace\-ratings ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-playlists ]
.RB [ \-\-preview | \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli carry\-stats
.RB [ \-\-from
.I path
.B \-\-to
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli write\-stats
.RB [ \-\-ratings ]
.RB [ \-\-play\-counts ]
.RB [ \-\-worker
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR path ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli queue
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli playlists
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli
.BR play\-pause " | " pause " | " resume " | " stop " | " next " | " previous
.br
.B helikodu\-cli seek
.I position
.br
.B helikodu\-cli volume
.RI [ level ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli shuffle
.I mode
.br
.B helikodu\-cli repeat
.I mode
.br
.B helikodu\-cli enqueue
.RB [ \-\-next ]
.IR file \&...
.br
.B helikodu\-cli enqueue
.RB [ \-\-next ]
.BI \-\-query " query"
.br
.B helikodu\-cli play\-query
.RB [ \-\-shuffle ]
.IR query \&...
.br
.B helikodu\-cli rate
.IR stars | none
.RB [ \-\-track
.IR id ]
.br
.B helikodu\-cli export\-playlist
.I playlist file
.br
.B helikodu\-cli \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B helikodu\-cli
is the command-line tool of Helikodu.
It plays files in the terminal, lists the audio devices, and scans and
queries the same library the desktop application uses.
These commands work on their own; the application need not be running.
The commands under
.B COMMANDS FOR THE RUNNING APPLICATION
control the running application over D-Bus instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS play
Plays the files in the order given.
Files of the same format join without a gap.
A file that cannot be opened or decoded is reported and skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " backend"
.B auto
(the default: PipeWire if it is running, otherwise ALSA),
.BR pipewire ,
.BR alsa ,
.B null
(discards the audio) or
.BR wav .
.TP
.BI \-\-device " id"
The device's stable name, as
.B list\-outputs
shows it: a PipeWire node name such as
.BR alsa_output.usb\-Topping_D10s\-00.analog\-stereo ,
or an ALSA PCM such as
.BR hw:CARD=D10s,DEV=0 .
The default is the backend's default device.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " mode"
.B shared
(the default) or
.BR exclusive .
.TP
.BI \-\-volume " n"
The position of the volume control, 0 to 100 (the default).
It follows the cubic curve of desktop mixers.
.TP
.BI \-\-wav\-out " path"
The file the
.B wav
backend writes; required with
.B \-\-backend wav
and refused otherwise.
The file is written as fast as the input decodes.
.TP
.BI \-\-replaygain " mode"
Loudness normalization by ReplayGain tags or Opus R128 tags:
.B off
(the default),
.BR track ,
.B album
or
.B auto
(the album gain when a neighbouring file in the list has the same album
title and album artists, the track gain otherwise).
A file without the chosen gain uses the other one; a file without either
plays unchanged.
A positive gain is lowered so that the tagged peak stays at or below full scale.
.TP
.BI \-\-preamp " dB"
Added to the gain of files with loudness tags, \-24 to 24 (default 0).
.PP
When standard input is a terminal, these keys control playback and a status
line on standard error shows the file, position, volume and output:
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume.
.TP
.BR n ", " p
Next file; previous file (restarts the current file when more than three
seconds of it have played).
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Seek back or forward 5 seconds.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Volume up or down by 5.
.TP
.B o
Move playback to the next output device, through the PipeWire and then the
ALSA devices, without stopping.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.PP
Otherwise the files play to the end without reading input, and a lost device
ends playback.
.B play
writes messages to standard error and nothing to standard output.
.SS list\-outputs
Lists the devices of every backend that plays sound (PipeWire and ALSA), or
of the one given with
.BR \-\-backend
.RB ( auto ,
.BR pipewire ,
.B alsa
or
.BR null ).
The default device is marked with
.BR * .
With
.B \-\-json
the output is a JSON array with an object per device:
.BR backend ,
.BR id ,
.BR description ,
.B is_default
and
.B capabilities
.RB ( sample_rates ,
.BR formats ,
.BR channel_counts ).
.SS scan
Adds the folders to the library and reads their new and changed files;
files that disappeared are marked missing.
Without folders, every folder already in the library is scanned again.
Progress goes to standard error, the summary to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " pattern"
Leaves out every file and folder whose name matches the pattern
.RB ( *
and
.B ?
are wildcards; case matters), or, when the pattern contains a
.BR / ,
the file or folder at that path.
May be given more than once.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " n"
The number of worker processes, 1 to 64.
The default is one per processor, at most 8.
.TP
.BI \-\-worker " path"
The scan worker program.
The default is
.B helikodu\-scan\-worker
beside
.B helikodu\-cli
or in
.I ../libexec/helikodu/
from it.
.SS search
Finds the tracks whose title, artists, album, album artists, genres,
composers or path contain every word of
.IR text ,
ignoring case, accents and character width, best matches first.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
At most
.I n
results, 1 to 1000 (default 50).
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " n"
Skips the first
.I n
results (default 0).
.SS info
Shows the tags, audio properties and loudness values of a file, read
directly, with its library entry and statistics when it is in the library.
An argument that is not an existing file is taken as a track number, as
.B search
prints it, and the track is shown from the library.
.SS stats
Shows the library folders, the totals and the most played tracks.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " n"
How many of the most played tracks to show, 0 to 1000 (default 10).
.SS loudness
Measures the loudness of library tracks (EBU R128, ITU-R BS.1770-4):
integrated loudness, loudness range, sample peak and true peak, and the
ReplayGain 2.0 gain relative to \-18 LUFS.
The tracks are given as files in the library or as track numbers.
The results are stored in the library, where playback prefers them over the
values in the tags.
Progress goes to standard error, the results to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-album
Measures the whole albums of the tracks given, with the album gain: the
album measured as one programme.
A track given without this option gets track values only.
.TP
.B \-\-library
Measures every library track that has no current measurement (never
measured, or its file changed since), with the other tracks of its album.
Takes no tracks.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-tags
Also writes the values into the files' tags (REPLAYGAIN_TRACK_GAIN,
REPLAYGAIN_TRACK_PEAK and the album pair).
Tracks of CUE sheets are not written.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " n"
The number of measuring threads, 1 to 64.
The default is half the processors.
.TP
.BI \-\-worker " path"
The scan worker program that reads written files again, as for
.BR scan .
.SS duplicates
Lists the groups of copies in the library: files with exactly the same
content.
Each group shows its main copy, the other copies, and files that are the same
file reached by another path (such as a hard link); missing files are
marked.
A summary line gives the number of groups and the size of the copies besides
the main copies.
Nothing is moved or deleted; the application's Find Duplicates window does
that.
.SS import
Imports play counts, ratings and playlists from another player:
.BR rhythmbox ,
.BR strawberry ,
.BR clementine ,
.B lollypop
or
.B itunes
(an exported Library.xml).
The player's files are only read; its databases are read from a copy.
Without
.B \-\-path
the file is looked for where the player keeps it, Flatpak folders included.
Entries are matched to library tracks by path, then by artist, title, album,
track number and a length within 2 seconds.
Without
.B \-\-apply
the command only shows what would change.
Play and skip counts are added (importing the same file again adds only the
plays made since); ratings are taken for unrated tracks only; the earliest
first and the latest last play win.
.TP
.BI \-\-path " path"
The player's library file, or the folder holding it.
.TP
.BI \-\-map " from" = to
A path prefix of the other library and the folder it is now.
A prefix with a drive letter is matched without regard to case.
May be given several times.
.TP
.B \-\-replace\-ratings
Takes the imported rating also for tracks that have one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-playlists
Leaves the playlists out.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Carries out the import, in one transaction.
.SS undo\-import
Undoes the newest import or carried statistics: counts lose what it added,
other values go back where they still hold what it set, and the playlists it
made are deleted.
.B \-\-list
lists the imports instead.
.SS export\-user\-data
Writes the ratings, play counts, history, playlists, smart playlists,
Favourites and saved searches to a JSON file, keyed by path and tags.
.SS import\-user\-data
Reads a file written by
.B export\-user\-data
into the library, with the options of
.BR import .
Counts take the higher value, so importing a file twice changes nothing.
.SS carry\-stats
Lists the missing files whose statistics, history and playlist entries a file
of the same recording (the same title and artist, a length within 2 seconds)
could take over.
With
.BR \-\-apply ,
carries them where there is one replacement; with
.B \-\-from
and
.BR \-\-to ,
carries them between the two files named.
.SS write\-stats
Writes the play counts and ratings that changed since they were last written
into the files' tags, as the
.B write_ratings_to_tags
and
.B write_play_counts_to_tags
settings say, or as
.B \-\-ratings
and
.B \-\-play\-counts
say.
.SH COMMANDS FOR THE RUNNING APPLICATION
These commands talk to the running Helikodu window through its D-Bus
interface,
.BR io.github.sorrelfox.Helikodu.Control1 .
They never start the application: when it is not running they say so and
end with exit status 4.
Playback asked for this way passes the same full-volume confirmation as in
the window.
.SS status
Shows the state, the playing track, the position, the volume, the play modes,
the place in the queue and the output.
.SS queue
Lists the queue in playing order; the current track is marked with
.BR > .
.SS playlists
Lists the playlists with their numbers, kinds and number of tracks.
.SS play\-pause, pause, resume, stop, next, previous
The transport.
.B previous
goes to the start of the track after its first seconds.
.SS seek
Moves to a
.I position
in the playing track, given in seconds
.RB ( 83 )
or as minutes and seconds
.RB ( 1:23 );
with
.B +
or
.B \-
in front it moves by that much
.RB ( +10 ", " \-5 ).
.SS volume
Without an argument prints the volume, 0 to 100.
With a
.IR level ,
0 to 100, sets it;
.B +5
and
.B \-5
change it by that much.
.SS shuffle
Sets the shuffle
.IR mode :
.BR off ", " tracks ", " albums ", " folders ", " groupings " or " within\-album .
.SS repeat
Sets the repeat
.IR mode :
.BR off ", " one " (the track), " album " or " all " (the queue)."
.SS enqueue
Adds files to the end of the queue, or with
.B \-\-next
after the playing track, and prints how many were added.
.TP
.BI \-\-query " query"
Adds the library tracks the query finds instead of files (at most 10,000).
The query is written as in the search field of the application, for example
.BR "genre:jazz rating>=4" ;
text without fields searches for its words.
.TP
.B \-\-next
Adds after the playing track instead of at the end.
.SS play\-query
Replaces the queue with the library tracks the query finds (the words given
are joined into one query) and plays them.
Finding none is an error and leaves the queue as it is.
.TP
.B \-\-shuffle
Plays them in random order.
.SS rate
Rates the playing library track with 0 to 5
.IR stars ,
or removes its rating with
.BR none .
.TP
.BI \-\-track " id"
Rates this library track, as
.B search
prints it, instead.
.SS export\-playlist
Writes a playlist, given by its name or its number as
.B playlists
prints them, to
.IR file ;
the extension picks the format:
.BR .m3u8 ", " .m3u ", " .pls " or " .xspf .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Prints the result as JSON.
Paths are given as text; a path that is not valid UTF-8 also has
.BR path_bytes ,
its exact bytes.
Times are seconds since the Unix epoch, lengths are milliseconds, and unknown
values are
.BR null .
Later versions may add keys; existing keys keep their meaning.
.TP
.BI \-\-database " path"
Uses this library database instead of the default one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints help for the tool or a command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Prints the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
For
.BR play ,
at least one file played; for
.BR scan ,
files that could not be read do not change the status;
.B search
without a match is a success.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error: the output could not be opened or failed, no backend could
be listed, there is no library yet, the library or a file could not be read,
a scan could not start, or
.B info
found no such track; for
.BR loudness ,
also a track that could not be measured or whose tags could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown option or value, or options that do not go together.
.TP
.B 3
.B play
could not play any of the files.
.TP
.B 4
A command for the running application found it not running, or found no
session bus.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
The library database is
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/helikodu/library.db
.RI ( ~/.local/share/helikodu/library.db
when it is not set).
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_COLLATE ", " LANG
The locale that sorting follows.
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus the commands for the running application use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/helikodu/library.db
The library database, shared with
.BR helikodu (1).
.B scan
creates it; the other library commands need it, except
.B info
on a file.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the ALSA devices, then play an album exclusively to one of them with
album gain:
.PP
.RS
.EX
helikodu\-cli list\-outputs \-\-backend alsa
helikodu\-cli play ~/Music/Album/*.flac \-\-backend alsa \e
    \-\-device \(aqhw:CARD=D10s,DEV=0\(aq \-\-mode exclusive \-\-replaygain album
.EE
.RE
.PP
Scan a folder and search it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
helikodu\-cli scan ~/Music \-\-exclude \(aq*.part\(aq
helikodu\-cli search miles davis \-\-limit 10 \-\-json
.EE
.RE
Play the best rated jazz of the library in the running application,
shuffled, then skip a track:
.PP
.RS
.EX
helikodu\-cli play\-query \-\-shuffle \(aqgenre:jazz rating>=4\(aq
helikodu\-cli next
helikodu\-cli status \-\-json
.EE
.RE
